.\" man/man3/Docv::Palette.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Palette" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Palette \- The colors of the terminal theme as RGB: the default foreground and background and the 256\-color palette.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Palette\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
The colors of the terminal theme as RGB: the default foreground and
background and the 256\-color palette. A terminal reports its theme in
answer to an OSC 21 query (\fB\%set\fR); until then xterm\(aqs values stand in,
on a black or white background for a dark or light scheme.
.PP
Colors can be ramped toward the foreground or the background, and
reduced to what the terminal shows.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
palette = Docv::Palette.new(dark: true)
palette.set("background", "rgb:28/2c/34")
palette.ramp(palette.background, 10) # 10% toward the foreground
.EE
.RE
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBANSI\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
ANSI = [
  {0, 0, 0},
  {205, 0, 0},
  {0, 205, 0},
  {205, 205, 0},
  {0, 0, 238},
  {205, 0, 205},
  {0, 205, 205},
  {229, 229, 229},
  {127, 127, 127},
  {255, 0, 0},
  {0, 255, 0},
  {255, 255, 0},
  {92, 92, 255},
  {255, 0, 255},
  {0, 255, 255},
  {255, 255, 255},
]
.EE
.RE
.PP
xterm\(aqs values of the 16 ANSI colors.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBCUBE = [0, 95, 135, 175, 215, 255]\fR
Channel levels of the 6\[u00D7]6\[u00D7]6 color cube (palette entries 16\-231).
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(dark : Bool = true)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse(value : String) : RGB | Nil\fR
Parses a color value of OSC 21: \fB\%rgb:r/g/b\fR (1\-4 hex digits per
channel, scaled), \fB\%#rgb\fR to \fB\%#rrrrggggbbbb\fR (most significant bits) or
\fB\%rgbi:r/g/b\fR (0.0\-1.0); an \fB\%@alpha\fR suffix is ignored. \fB\%nil\fR for an
empty or unknown value.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.standard(index : Int32) : RGB\fR
xterm\(aqs value of palette entry \fIindex\fR.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef background : RGB\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef dark? : Bool\fR
True when the background is dark.
.PP
\fBdef foreground : RGB\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef ramp(rgb : RGB, percent : Int32) : RGB\fR
\fIrgb\fR moved \fIpercent\fR toward the foreground (positive) or the
background (negative).
.TP 4
\fBdef reduce(color : Color, depth : ColorDepth) : Color\fR
\fIcolor\fR as the terminal shows it at \fIdepth\fR: RGB colors, and palette
entries past the ANSI colors at \fB\%ColorDepth::Ansi\fR, become the nearest
palette entry; at \fB\%ColorDepth::None\fR every color is the default.
.TP 4
\fBdef reported? : Bool\fR
True once the terminal reported a color.
.TP 4
\fBdef rgb(color : Color, foreground : Bool) : RGB\fR
The RGB value of \fIcolor\fR as a foreground or background.
.TP 4
\fBdef set(key : String, value : String) : Bool\fR
Sets the color of an OSC 21 \fIkey\fR (\fB\%foreground\fR, \fB\%background\fR or a
palette index) from \fIvalue\fR; false for keys and values it does not
take.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/palette.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::ColorDepth" (3cr),
.BR "Docv::Palette::RGB" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
